{# #### `project_attributes_setting_booking_check_availability_url` #}

{{SetCustomerMetadataAttribute(
    idn="project_attributes_setting_booking_check_availability_url",
    field="multiple_fields",
    value={ "title": "4-26. Booking - Check Availability - Link (URL) [B] [IMPORTANT]", "description": """This setting stores the URL used during availability checks in hospitality booking flows.

**Best Practice:** In default hospitality mode, provide your exact Google Maps business URL when
your hotel name is not unique. If you use endpoint mode, use a stable HTTPS endpoint and ensure it
matches your selected request method and headers. If your hotel name is unique and Google matches it
reliably, leaving this empty in default mode is acceptable.

Use this especially when:

- Multiple properties share similar names.
- Guests use a different spelling than your listing.
- Name-only matching may select the wrong property.

Examples:

- `https://maps.app.goo.gl/e14ZDSGkr3ps534x7`
- `https://api.yourhotel.com/availability`

To capture a Google Maps business link, open the property in Google Maps, choose `Share`, and copy
the guest-facing link.

---

**⚙️ Technical & System Details (Advanced)**

**System Usage:** In hospitality default availability processing, this URL is passed as
`businessUrl` in the request payload to improve property matching while `project_business_name` is
used as `hotelName`. In endpoint-based availability modes, runtime sends requests directly to this
URL (`GET` with query parameters or `POST` with request body) using configured request headers.

**Fallbacks:** If empty in default hospitality mode, availability checks still run using
`project_business_name` as the matching key, which can be ambiguous for non-unique names. If runtime
dispatch requires HTTP endpoint calling and this field is empty, validation fails and availability
checking cannot proceed until the URL is configured.

**Dependencies:**

- **Primary Settings:**
  - `project_attributes_setting_booking_check_availability_type`: Controls whether this field is
    interpreted as default-map disambiguation URL or endpoint URL.
  - `project_attributes_setting_booking_check_availability_request_http_method`: Defines how this
    URL is called in endpoint mode (`GET` or `POST`).
  - `project_attributes_setting_booking_check_availability_request_headers`: Supplies headers for
    endpoint requests sent to this URL.
  - `project_business_name`: Used as the default fallback identifier when this URL is empty.
- **Logic Interactions:**
  - `project_attributes_setting_booking_check_availability_enabled`: Availability-check logic must
    be active for this URL to be used.""", "group": "4. Agent Behavior", "is_hidden": False }
)}}

